  "context_pill": "Tax Liability Calculation (Old Regime)",
  "example_summary": "Mr. Arjun's tax liability at different ages (52, 64, 83) for a total income of ₹ 16,00,000 under the regular regime for A.Y. 2026-27.",
  "source_provision": "| Category | Age Threshold | Basic Exemption Limit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Resident Individual | Below 60 Years | ₹ 2,50,000 |\n| Senior Citizen | 60 - 80 Years | ₹ 3,00,000 |\n| Super Senior Citizen | Above 80 Years | ₹ 5,00,000 |\n\n\n### Progressive Tax Slab Rates (Regular Regime)\n* **0 - 2.5/3/5 Lakhs**: Nil rate.\n* **Next Slab (up to 5 Lakhs)**: 5% (Not applicable for Super Senior Citizens).\n* **5 Lakhs to 10 Lakhs**: 20%.\n* **Above 10 Lakhs**: 30%.\n\n\n> [!NOTE] Health and Education Cess: A mandatory surcharge of 4% is levied on the total income tax computed, applicable to all categories regardless of age.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Opt-out Clause: Taxpayers choosing to shift out of the default tax regime u/s 115BAC must compute tax liability based on these traditional slab structures.",
